 No, it was not established as a religious organization. The organization was established in 1909 by both white and Negro leaders to promote the advancement of African Americans, with the goal of achieving equal rights for all Americans.

How many members are there in the NAACP? More than 350,000 members are located in almost every state, the District of Columbia, and Alaska. More than 50% of the members are in the seventeen southern and border states.

How many regional offices were established by the NAACP? Three regional offices have been established: in Atlanta, Georgia; Dallas, Texas (currently closed by a court injunction) ;
